From: NumberOneGit rpi5-uefi contributors
Date: Sun, 17 Aug 2026 13:00:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Platform/RaspberryPi, Silicon/Broadcom: RPi5 port (changed files)

The RPi5 port's modifications and deletions of files that exist upstream.
The port's ADDED files ship separately as this recipe's files/edk2-platforms/
overlay, copied into the tree during do_unpack BEFORE this and the later
patches apply.

Scope is limited to the package trees this build actually compiles
(Platform/RaspberryPi, Silicon/Broadcom, Silicon/RaspberryPi).

ORIGIN AND REBASE HISTORY
  Originally extracted from the retired NumberOneGit/edk2-platforms fork at
  4e426104a, as its delta against that fork's merge-base with upstream
  (80ee8b861, 2024-03-12), and carried against that 2024 base.

  Rebased onto upstream master 9ef9bcef5 (2026-08-21) when the edk2 recipe
  moved to edk2-stable202608, which the 2024 base could not build against.
  The rebase shrank the patch from 43 changed files to 24: upstream has since
  absorbed, independently, most of what the fork had changed. Five files
  conflicted and were resolved as follows.

    MmcDebug.c                  kept the port's "#if !defined(MDEPKG_NDEBUG)"
                                guard around mStrUnit/mStrValue. Upstream
                                leaves them unguarded, but they are referenced
                                only inside DEBUG(), which compiles away under
                                MDEPKG_NDEBUG -- so a RELEASE build without the
                                guard trips -Werror=unused-variable.
    PlatformBootManagerLib.inf  dropped the port's empty [FeaturePcd] section.
    PlatformBm.c                dropped a whitespace-only change.
    FdtDxe.c                    kept the port's switch from
                                PcdGet32 (PcdFdtBaseAddress) to
                                FdtPlatformGetBase () plus the BoardInfoLib
                                revision lookup -- the RPi5 port's whole reason
                                for touching this driver.
    RpiFirmwareDxe.c            kept all ten of the port's hunks: the runtime
                                mMboxBaseAddress in place of the hardcoded
                                BCM2836_MBOX_BASE_ADDRESS, the RTC tag structs,
                                the EfiAtRuntime cache maintenance around the
                                DMA buffer, the GCD mapping of the mailbox page,
                                and the deletion of the five model-name/family
                                helpers (they moved to BoardRevisionHelperLib,
                                which the overlay supplies; nothing in the tree
                                still references them).

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [platform port carried out-of-tree]
